  "english": "On the feast of Martyrs and other common saints who do not have a proper blessing: from the Tone of the day, say the Martyrs' \"The Lord in heaven\" [Ter yerknits], and then one more Hymn of other saints according to the propriety of the day; and after the Coming of the Spirit, and the rest according to order.\n\nMonday. Tone 3 [gd]: Of the holy Infants of Bethlehem, and of Akakios the witness, and of Movkima the priest, and of Kodratos the soldier. Canticle [Harts] Tone 3 [dg]: \"Today the innocent holy\" with its proper parts. Midday Liturgy Psalm 8: \"Out of the mouths of babes\". Proverbs 29:2 \"In praise of\" to verse 7 \"righteous minds\". Prophet Isaiah 18:7 \"In that time\" to verse 7 \"Mount Zion\". Apostle Hebrews 2:14 \"Forasmuch then\" to verse 18 \"to succor\". Alleluia: \"The Lord loveth justice\". Gospel Matthew 2:16 \"Then when he saw\" to verse 18 \"because they were not\".\n\nTuesday. Tone 8 [gk]: Of the holy virgins Nune and Mane. Say the Blessing, the Canticle [Harts], and all the rest of Saint Hripsime. Midday Liturgy Introit: \"Betrothed of Christ\". Psalm 44 [45]: \"They shall be brought\". Book of Song of Songs 8:14 \"Flee, my beloved\" to verse 24 \"spotless\". Prophet Isaiah 27:11 \"Women who come\" to verse 13 \"in Jerusalem\". Catholic Epistle 1 Peter 5:8 \"Be sober\" to verse 11 \"forever, amen\". Alleluia: \"She shall stand\". Gospel John 12:24 \"Verily, verily\" to verse 26 \"him my Father\".\n\nWednesday. Tone 2 [bd]: Canticle [Harts] Tone 3 [gd]: \"Who co-eternal\". Midday Liturgy Psalm 65 [66]: \"Save Thy servants\". Apostle Romans 4:13 \"For not if\" to verse 22 \"unto righteousness\". Alleluia: \"My heart was troubled\". Gospel Matthew 10:34 \"Think not\" to verse 42 \"his reward\".\n\nAnd regarding the Martyrs' Canticles [Harts], know this:\nFrom this Thursday, make a beginning from the first Tone to the last Tone, and say them in order; and when they end, begin again. But Tone 3 [gd] \"Who boundless\", Tone 8 [gk] \"The military hosts\", and Tone 4 [dd] \"Who participated\" — do not say these three Canticles in order, because they have their own proper days.\n\nThursday. Tone 4 [bk]: Of the holy princes Sahak and Joseph, and the witnesses Sarkis and Bakhos. Blessing [of the Tone] of the Martyrs. Canticle [Harts] Tone 1 [ad]: \"Thee the righteous\". Midday Liturgy Psalm 115 [116]: \"Precious is\", Response: \"I believed\". Proverbs 6:1 \"My son, if thou be\" to verse 5 \"from the snares\". Prophet Isaiah 33:5 \"Holy is the Lord\" to verse 8 \"them among men\". Apostle Romans 8:18 \"For I reckon\" to verse 27 \"for the saints\". Alleluia: \"The righteous cried\". Gospel Luke 21:12 \"But before\" to verse 19 \"your souls\".\n\nFriday. Tone 1 [ad]: Canticle [Harts] of Rest Tone 3 [gd]: \"Who art the King\". Midday Liturgy Psalm 97 [98]: \"Have seen all\". Apostle Romans 5:12 \"For as by one\" to verse 21 \"our Lord\". Alleluia: \"For Thy name's sake\". Gospel Matthew 11:25 \"At that time\" to verse 30 \"faint-hearted\".\n\nSaturday. Tone 8 [gk]: Of the holy ones Nerses the Great, our patriarch, and Khat the bishop. Blessing Tone 4 [bk]: \"Who the unutterable light\". Canticle [Harts] Tone 3 [gd]: \"Today the church celebrates\" with its proper parts. Midday Liturgy Psalm 131 [132]: \"Priests\". Wisdom of Solomon 2:23 \"For God\" to 3:8 \"forever\". Prophet Isaiah 57:15 \"Thus saith the high\" to verse 16 \"I made\". Apostle Hebrews 13:7 \"Remember your leaders\" to verse 9 \"so walked\". Alleluia: \"Thy priests\". Gospel Matthew 10:16 \"Behold, I\" to verse 22 \"he shall stand\". In the Evening: \"Joyful Light\", and the rest according to order.\n\nFourth Sunday after the Coming of the Spirit. Tone 4 [dd]: Canticle [Harts] Tone 1 [ad]: \"Be Thou brightened\". Magnificat [Metsatsustse] Tone 1 [ad]: \"Who wast chosen from the beginning\". Midday Liturgy Psalm 64 [65]: \"To Thee is due\". Prophet Isaiah 1:1 \"Hear, O heaven\" to verse 15 \"are full of blood\". Psalm: \"Holy is Thy temple\". Apostle Romans 6:12 \"Let not therefore\" to verse 23 \"in our Lord\". Alleluia: \"Thou hast been pleased, Lord\". Gospel Matthew 12:1 \"At that time went\" to verse 8 \"Son of man\". In the Evening, Messedi: \"Let Thy hand be\", \"Who shepherdest\". Dismissal Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 4 [dd]: \"Glorifier\". Proclamation: \"Let us ask\", \"Save us\". Prayer: \"King of peace\". And then the Fast of Saint Gregory our Illuminator; but there are feasts.",
